eds a ticket in person/review after a ready report, a completed or merged one, or a dropped one whose matched rule asks for a closing message. IM limit: 100 words."), "name": String("orchestrator_reply"), "parameters": Object {"$schema": String("https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema"), "additionalProperties": Bool(false), "properties": Object {"human_action": Object {"description": String("Required for attention: the ticket's current attention question."), "minLength": Number(1), "type": String("string")}, "purpose": Object {"enum": Array [String("answer"), String("result"), String("attention")], "type": String("string")}, "text": Object {"maxLength": Number(20000), "minLength": Number(1), "type": String("string")}, "ticket_id": Object {"type": String("string")}, "trigger_id": Object {"description": String("The original human question, for an answer only."), "type": String("string")}}, "required": Array [String("purpose"), String("text")], "type": String("object")}}, "type": String("function")}, Object {"function": Object {"description": String("Route candidates, one item each by the card's trigger_id, in one call: accept an explicit request as a new ticket, attach a trigger to an existing ticket, stop a ticket on a person's stop message, or ignore a candidate that needs no ticket or stop, as dispatch says. Items run in order and each is answered on its own; a refused item leaves the others. An inferred candidate may be ignored here; accepting one goes through orchestrator_eval_decide."), "name": String("orchestrator_route"), "parameters": Object {"$schema": String("https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema"), "additionalProperties": Bool(false), "properties": Object {"decisions": Object {"items": Object {"additionalProperties": Bool(false), "properties": Object {"acknowledgement": Object {"description": String("accept: one brief sentence of at most 100 words naming the concrete change and intended result in the source language. It is posted as a reply to 